# A project of its own: `mix.lock` is committed, because an example that
# resolves differently every time it is opened is one that stops working
# quietly, and the trees it resolves into are not.
/_build/
/deps/
/cover/
/doc/
*.tar
erl_crash.dump

# The window's crate is an application, so its lock is source rather than output —
# and what the crate builds is neither: `target/` is the toolchain's, and
# `gen/` is what `tauri-build` writes on every compile.
!/app/Cargo.lock
/app/target/
/app/gen/
